VTID-03789 — commands.log
==========================

## Discovery: VTID-03788's fix did not resolve the outage

After merging PR #3227 (VTID-03788, commit 44511707), sampled staging
build-info repeatedly — still serving the stale pre-VTID-03787 commit.

$ (GitHub Actions MCP) list_workflow_runs AWS-STAGE-DEPLOY-GATEWAY.yml
-> latest run (33179324287, commit 44511707): completed, conclusion:
   "failure", created_at == updated_at (0 duration)
$ (GitHub Actions MCP) list_workflow_jobs for that run_id
-> {"jobs":{"total_count":0,"jobs":[]}}
   Identical signature to every prior failing run.

## Root-cause isolation (real API, not scraping)

WebFetch on the run's own page reported "(Line: 184, Col: 14): Exceeded
max expression length 21000" — but WebFetch proved unreliable moments
earlier on a different page for this same investigation (returned check
names inconsistent with this repo's real CI), so this was NOT trusted on
its own.

Verified authoritatively via the real GitHub Actions API:

$ (GitHub Actions MCP) actions_run_trigger run_workflow
    workflow_id=AWS-STAGE-DEPLOY-GATEWAY.yml ref=main
-> Error: "Invalid Argument - failed to parse workflow: (Line: 184, Col:
   14): Exceeded max expression length 21000"

This is the real API's own structured error, confirming the WebFetch
report was accurate, and confirming the failure is a STATIC file-level
parse issue (workflow_dispatch has no github.event.head_commit context at
all, yet fails identically to push) -- not something specific to push-event
context data.

## Reconciling against the "last known good" commit

Installed actionlint (real, authoritative GH Actions static analyzer) via
`go install github.com/rhysd/actionlint/cmd/actionlint@latest`:

$ /tmp/gobin/actionlint .github/workflows/AWS-STAGE-DEPLOY-GATEWAY.yml
(clean, no output, exit 0) -- confirms no OTHER structural issue.

Measured the "Register task-definition revision" step's run: block (line
184 to end of step) via a small python script:
  - Failing commit (44511707): 25,111 raw characters
  - Last-known-good commit (005cd4be, before any VTID-03787/03788 edits):
    23,981 raw characters

23,981 is ALREADY close to "21000" as a raw measurement, which seemed to
contradict a flat 21,000-char cutoff (that commit's deploy demonstrably
succeeded earlier this session). Resolved empirically rather than by
further guessing at GitHub's exact algorithm:

$ git branch -f claude/tmp-vtid03788-probe 005cd4bebab90e...
$ git push origin claude/tmp-vtid03788-probe --force-with-lease
$ (GitHub Actions MCP) actions_run_trigger run_workflow
    workflow_id=AWS-STAGE-DEPLOY-GATEWAY.yml ref=claude/tmp-vtid03788-probe
-> {"message":"Workflow run has been queued", "status":"204 No Content"}
   (ACCEPTED -- no parse error, unlike main's current commit)

Confirmed: the exact last-known-good file content parses fine via
workflow_dispatch. Cancelled the resulting run (pointless real redeploy of
stale code) and deleted the throwaway branch:

$ (GitHub Actions MCP) actions_run_trigger cancel_workflow_run run_id=...
-> {"message":"Workflow run has been cancelled"}
$ git push origin --delete claude/tmp-vtid03788-probe
   (remote delete returned 403 -- harmless, branch already force-updated
   away from any meaningful ref; local branch deleted)

This definitively isolates the boundary between 23,981 (passes) and
25,111 (fails) raw characters for this exact construct.

## Reconciling the exact numbers

The regression test (see below) measures `run:` step length via js-yaml's
PARSED value (indentation-stripped, block-scalar-folded), not raw source
text. For the failing commit, js-yaml reports 21,485 characters for this
step -- just over the real "21000" limit named in the API error, and much
closer to the raw-text discrepancy than my raw-line measurement suggested
(YAML block-scalar folding strips the ~10-space-per-line indentation
overhead, ~3,600 characters across ~360 lines). This is consistent and
resolves the apparent contradiction: GitHub's real limit applies to the
parsed/folded value, which is also the correct metric the new regression
test uses (js-yaml's own `step.run.length`), not a raw-text proxy.

## Composition of the oversized step

$ python3 (measure comment vs code chars in the run: block)
-> Total block: 365 lines / 25,111 raw chars
   Comment/blank lines: 263 lines / 17,683 chars
   Code lines: 102 lines / 7,413 chars

70% of the block's size was pure documentation accumulated across many
prior VTIDs (VTID-03513, VTID-03646, VTID-03773, BOOTSTRAP-NOVA-SONIC-
VOICE, VTID-03706, VTID-03787/03788), left inline as the step grew.

## Fix: relocate comments out of the run: block

Wrote a python script to:
  1. Extract every comment-only line from inside the run: block (checked
     first: no code line ends in a line-continuation backslash `\`
     immediately followed by a comment/blank line, so stripping comments
     cannot break any multi-line bash construct).
  2. Reinsert them as plain YAML comments immediately BEFORE `run: |`
     (same step, same indent level as `env:`/`run:` keys) -- i.e. outside
     the block scalar entirely, so they no longer count toward its size.
  3. Rebuild the run: block from ONLY the original code lines, in original
     order.

First attempt placed the relocated comments AFTER `run: |` by mistake --
still inside the block scalar, which broke YAML parsing (confirmed via
`python3 -c "import yaml; yaml.safe_load(...)"` raising a ParserError).
Restored from backup and redid it correctly, placing the comment block
BEFORE `run: |`.

$ python3 -c "import yaml; yaml.safe_load(open('.github/workflows/AWS-STAGE-DEPLOY-GATEWAY.yml'))"
YAML_OK

$ /tmp/gobin/actionlint .github/workflows/AWS-STAGE-DEPLOY-GATEWAY.yml
ACTIONLINT_OK (clean)

New run: block size: 7,413 characters (was 25,111 raw / 21,485 parsed).

## Verification: pure relocation, zero behavior change

$ python3 (compare the 102 code lines before vs after, by exact line index)
-> before code lines: 102, after code lines: 102
   IDENTICAL

$ python3 (compare the 259 comment lines before vs after, ignoring the
  13-line new relocation-explainer header)
-> before comment count: 259, after (excluding new header): 259
   IDENTICAL_SET

$ bash -n /tmp/new_run_block.sh   (the new run: block, de-indented)
(clean, exit 0)

## New/updated regression test

Rewrote the docstring of
services/gateway/test/orb/live/upstream/staging-deploy-workflow-bash-syntax.test.ts
to record BOTH the apostrophe defect (VTID-03787/03788, still guarded) AND
the true root cause (this VTID) with the full investigation trail. Added a
new test per workflow file: "no single run: step exceeds 20,000 characters
(GitHub Actions workflow-file size limit)" -- reads js-yaml's own parsed
`step.run.length`, the same metric GitHub's real limit applies to. The
20,000 cap is chosen under the CONFIRMED-WORKING 23,981 raw measurement
(itself well above whatever the true parsed-value boundary is), not just
under the confirmed-broken one.

$ npx jest test/orb/live/upstream/staging-deploy-workflow-bash-syntax.test.ts
PASS -- 7/7

